  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Friday) \nIssued at 1104 PM CDT Fri May 29 2026\n\nSunday into Monday, upper level ridging will develop over Texas, \npushing our highs in the mid 90s to near 100 degrees, with the \nhottest temperatures across the Big Country. \n\nFrom Tuesday through the end of the week, the ridge is expected \nto gradually weaken, and likely being replaced by weak upper level\ntroughing from Wednesday through the end of the work week, \nallowing for cooler afternoon highs. Tuesday, we'll see upper 80s \ninto the mid 90s, and then mid 80s to lower 90s from Wednesday \nthrough Friday. In addition to the cooler temperatures, there will\nbe a low to medium (20%-50%) chance for showers and thunderstorms\neach day, mainly from Wednesday into next weekend. However, with \nthe upper level troughing expected to be weak, and timing of any \nupper level disturbances still unclear, there is quite a bit of \nuncertainty regarding the coverage and intensity of any showers \nand thunderstorms in our area.",
